 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "America almost turned Louisiana's swamps into hippo ranches.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.511
  },
  {
   "text": "The plan: hippos eat the weeds, then Americans eat the hippos.",
   "s": 3.811,
   "e": 6.728
  },
  {
   "text": "The weed was water hyacinth, a purple flower from an 1884 New Orleans fair.",
   "s": 7.028,
   "e": 11.851
  },
  {
   "text": "It spread so fast that boats got stuck in the bayous.",
   "s": 12.151,
   "e": 14.505
  },
  {
   "text": "Meanwhile, America was running short of meat.",
   "s": 14.805,
   "e": 16.775
  },
  {
   "text": "So in 1910, Congressman Robert Broussard wrote a bill: import hippos. Two problems, one animal.",
   "s": 17.075,
   "e": 23.08
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it got stranger.",
   "s": 23.38,
   "e": 24.365
  },
  {
   "text": "His star witnesses had been enemies in a war in Africa. One later became a German spy.",
   "s": 24.665,
   "e": 29.761
  },
  {
   "text": "Now they teamed up to sell Congress on hippos.",
   "s": 30.061,
   "e": 32.145
  },
  {
   "text": "A government expert said hippos could add a million tons of meat a year.",
   "s": 32.445,
   "e": 35.968
  },
  {
   "text": "He said hippo tasted like pork and beef combined.",
   "s": 36.268,
   "e": 38.727
  },
  {
   "text": "The New York Times called it \"lake cow bacon.\"",
   "s": 39.027,
   "e": 41.119
  },
  {
   "text": "Imagine ordering a hippo burger in New Orleans.",
   "s": 41.299,
   "e": 43.498
  },
  {
   "text": "Even Theodore Roosevelt backed the idea.",
   "s": 43.798,
   "e": 45.732
  },
  {
   "text": "So where are Louisiana's hippos?",
   "s": 46.032,
   "e": 47.37
  },
  {
   "text": "Nowhere. The bill died in committee, and not one hippo ever arrived.",
   "s": 47.79,
   "e": 51.083
  },
  {
   "text": "But hippos did make it to the Americas. Pablo Escobar kept four at his zoo in Colombia.",
   "s": 51.383,
   "e": 56.482
  },
  {
   "text": "Today, well over a hundred of their descendants roam wild.",
   "s": 56.782,
   "e": 59.628
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow for a new weird true story every day.",
   "s": 59.928,
   "e": 61.965
  }
 ],
